# 158. Final Portfolio Narrative

PocketLedger should ultimately tell this engineering story:

I started with the financial domain instead of the UI.

Money is represented exactly.

Balances are derived rather than duplicated.

Income, expenses and internal transfers have explicit semantics.

Then I built a typed native networking layer using URLSession and async/await.

Authentication sessions are secured in Keychain and refreshed through an actor-isolated session manager.

PostgreSQL is the remote source of truth.

SwiftData provides local cached reads.

Repositories coordinate remote and local state.

Views only render presentation state.

Business logic is independently tested.

Face ID protects local access.

Swift Charts visualizes data generated by tested domain calculations.

Failures, offline behavior, accessibility and Dark Mode are treated as product requirements rather than final polish.

Finally, the application is distributed through TestFlight and documented as a real engineering project.

That is the story the repository should communicate.

